    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0304" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg224"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-06-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 598.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instruction No. 644,
                    of the 29th ultimo, relating to the action of Mr. Pickerell, our consul at St.
                    Michaels, Azores, in taking charge of the British consulate during the proposed
                    absence of the British consul, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of a
                    note from the foreign office, dated the 19th instant, conveying the thanks of
                    His Majesty’s Government for the courtesy of the United States Government in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d220-a1.xml" xpointer="d220-a1"/>
